      "writtenOn": "2025-04-15T23:41:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this might be wrong? IIUC, this happens if a single queue/device is lost, but we will end up marking every future (potentially unrelated futures on other queue/devices) ready here.\n\nI think this isn\u0027t a problem atm for `WaitAny` with a timeout because we only allow a single queue/device, but I think that if we are just polling with `timeout\u003d0`, this could happen? This is where I think I thought we would need the indices to events on a specific queue so that we can properly set those to be ready, but not others.\n\nSeparately though... I\u0027m wondering whether we even need to do this?... If the device is lost, I think it will result in `ExecutionQueueBase::AssumeCommandsComplete` being called here https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/Device.cpp;l\u003d710;drc\u003df667feb8a5c6f227b49328ce78a062acc4f81187;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1 and IIUC, that should set the completed serial of the corresponding queue to the end, which in turn should result in the `PollFutures` below seeing the queue events as `IsReadyToComplete()`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 178,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 181,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "7793c72883e4bba0c91aeafaee0fff1fbdd47751",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
